<!--
    Late common-subexpression elimination (`option latecse on|off`, default
    off; P3 simplification-quiescence, `kuna_latecse`) and the weight form of
    `impliedrefs` (`option impliedrefs <n>:<w>`; P6 explicit-marking,
    `ActionMarkExplicit`).

    Hand-written x86-64 (nasm): `twice` computes (a + b) * c once before a call and again after
    it, from callee-saved registers, and returns the call's result plus the
    second copy; `small` computes a + b once into rbx and passes it to three
    calls before returning it.

    Pass 1 is the shipped default: the two copies in `twice` print twice, and
    `small`'s sum, read four times, is declared as a temporary. Pass 2 turns
    `latecse` on: the second copy in `twice` reads the first. Pass 3 sets
    `impliedrefs 2:8`: `small`'s two-term sum read four times (weight 8)
    prints at every use instead of being declared.
-->
